From 4a4a8039ca731da576d8f2d2e1637459d1e207c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 11:29:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] webui: the Professional page drops WiFi 7 Mode and Wireless
 Mode

Both rows were per RADIO on a page that writes wl<unit>_<key> bare through one
generic apply, and neither setting is owned per radio.

WiFi 7 (11be) is chosen per NETWORK on the Network menu: sdn.js builds the
wifi7_11be switch on SDN.asp and couples it to the security mode in both
directions - turning it on force-selects an SAE-capable auth, and choosing a
non-SAE auth while it is on warns first. The linked General tab carries the same
coupling. This page had none of it, so it could raise 11be on one radio while the
crypto stayed unable to advertise EHT, and it synced nothing to the other bands.

Wireless Mode (nmode_x) sets 11ax=0 at bringup for "N only"
(rc/sysdeps/init-broadcom.c:11312), which drops HE and therefore EHT. Field
report 2026-09-18: a GT-BE98 whose 2.4 GHz radio reported HT only - no HE or EHT
MCS, OFDM-only rates - so the client was correctly showing no Wi-Fi 6 or 7 badge
on that band. The row is per radio but nothing links it to the surface that owns
it, so the same key was editable from two unlinked places.

RWFP_20..RWFP_23 ("N only" / "Legacy" / "AX only" / "N / AC / AX mixed") were
referenced only by the removed Wireless Mode row and are dropped from all 25
packs. The packs are name-keyed KEY=value, not positional, so removal shifts
nothing; dict-lockstep holds at 6987 lines.

KNOWN CONSEQUENCE: nmode_x now has no linked UI. The General tab does not carry
it and neither does the Network menu; the only shipped page that does is the
stock Advanced_WAdvanced_Content.asp, which ships unlinked. A box already forced
to N only needs:
  nvram set wl<2.4 unit>_nmode_x=0 && nvram commit && service restart_wireless
On quad-band models the 2.4 GHz radio is wl3, not wl0.

Gates: reaper_static_checks 13/13 (dict-lockstep 25 @ 6987), reaper_langcheck
0 breakers / 25 pages, test_js_parse 25/25, reaper_hiddencheck clean.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
